WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.200
John Wick could have been just another action
movie, but what audiences got was something

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.140
else entirely.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.860
John Wick: Chapter 3 - Parabellum hits theaters
May 17, and promises to take viewers even

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.500
deeper into the world of assassins and their
various vendettas.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.990
Here's what you should watch before you head
to the theater.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.890
There's a lot of great dialogue in the first
John Wick film, but we all know which one

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.520
is the true money line:

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:30.100
"People keep asking if I'm back and I haven't
really had an answer… but now, yeah, I'm

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.680
thinking I'm back!"

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.470
It's as much a statement about the character
of John Wick as it is a battle cry for Keanu

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.340
Reeves the actor.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.540
Reeves had a string of hits in the '90s, including
a little movie you might've heard of called

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.400
The Matrix, but then came the sequels.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.680
After their mixed reception, it seemed like
Keanu's star was finally descending.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.600
He continued to work on smaller films and
passion projects, but he didn't truly rise

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.260
to prominence again until 2014, when he donned
a suit and dug up a lockbox full of guns and

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.720
gold coins in John Wick.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:05.380
Reeves was back in the spotlight with plenty
of momentum, and will even be returning to

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:10.000
his first iconic role in the long awaited
Bill and Ted Face the Music alongside Alex

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:10.540
Winter.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.800
Yeah, we're thinking he's back.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.840
The first entry in the John Wick franchise
is incredibly straightforward.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.880
For those who haven't seen it — spoiler
alert — a man named John Wick who has recently

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.240
lost his wife learns that she had adopted
a puppy for him.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.680
He takes the puppy in and loves it with all
of his heart for a single day.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.300
But after a chance run-in with the dirtbag
son of a mob boss, things go wrong.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.820
That dirtbag son decides he wants John's car,
so he goes and takes it, and in the process,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.120
he kills John's dog.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.980
This is a big mistake,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.800
"May I ask why?"

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.680
"Yeah, well.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:50.480
Cuz he stole John Wick’s car, sir, and…
uh, killed his dog."

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.470
Turns out, John is a retired assassin who
was so good at his job that he's essentially

00:01:55.470 --> 00:02:00.170
the boogeyman for other hired killers, and
he's mad enough about his dead doggy to get

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.400
back in the game and destroy everything in
his path until he gets his revenge.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.620
It's a simple story, but it's told incredibly
well.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.100
Smash cut to John Wick Chapter 2, and we learn
a lot more about the secretive world of the

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:12.640
assassins.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.840
This globetrotting adventure introduces a
high council of assassins and criminal masterminds

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.060
— some of whom have unfinished business
with John Wick himself.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.060
Enter Santino D'Antonio, who has a favor to
call in.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.160
"...no."

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.300
The job is simple: kill D'Antonio's sister,
Gianna so that he can take her seat at the

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.380
table of the high council.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.000
John goes through with it and immediately
becomes entangled in a conspiracy that leads

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.320
to D'Antonio placing a massive contract on
John's head to cover his tracks.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:55.240
The hunt for John Wick escalates to the point
where John is forced to kill someone on the

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:55.680
grounds of the Continental, which is a big
no-no.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.640
By the end of Chapter 2, Wick is on the run
with a one-hour head start to outrun every

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.980
assassin in the world, leading to the events
of Chapter 3.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.180
As much as we love the specially-minted gold
coins used by the the killers in John Wick's

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.300
world, there's another currency that's just
as important: blood markers.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:17.459
They're one of the few things that reign in
even the most brutal and relentless of hired

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:21.800
killers, and a blood marker is only earned
when another assassin does someone an immense

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.340
favor.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.960
They can then claim that marker at any time
to call in any favor in return.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.620
It cannot be refused — it's taken as seriously
as spilling blood within the halls of the

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.140
Continental.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.200
"Rules."

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.140
"Exactly: rules."

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.510
The reason John had to take the job to kill
a member of the High Table was a marker held

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:47.209
by Santino D'Antonio — one that he earned
by helping John get out of the assassin's

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:51.849
life, and go live his fairy tale existence
with his wife in peace before the events of

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:52.380
the first film.

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:56.959
By the end of Chapter 2, as John Wick goes
to take his head start in escaping with an

00:03:56.959 --> 00:04:02.090
open contract for $14 million on his head,
Winston gives him a blood marker which may

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.680
act as his only lifeline now that he's been
made excommunicado from the league of assassins.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.900
In the first two John Wick films, we've already
seen a seen an incredible roster of over-the-top

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.769
characters populating the shadowy, stylish
underworld where anyone could be an assassin

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:19.700
just waiting for the right moment to strike.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:25.080
That doesn't seem likely to change as we get
into Chapter 3, with both returning characters

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.400
and some brand-new faces.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:32.360
Ian McShane will be back as Winston, the manager
of the Continental, and Keanu's Matrix co-star,

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.080
Laurence Fishburne, will be returning as the
mysterious Bowery King, a seemingly homeless

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.100
man with a deep knowledge of the world of
Assassins and a love of pigeons.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.090
"Seven million dollars?

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.080
Damn!

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.040
It’s Christmas.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.620
We're going to Applebee's after this!"

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.300
Here's hoping that the minds behind the John
Wick franchise can find a place for Carrie-Anne

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.720
Moss, if she's interested, completing the
— ahem — Trinity.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.740
Seeing the three stars of The Matrix reunited
on screen, even for a short time, would be

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.620
pretty awesome.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:07.060
As for the new characters, Parabellum has
upped the ante with an impressive roster of

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:07.580
stars.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:12.140
Halle Berry will appear as Sofia, a former
accomplice of John's who wields two pistols

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:17.380
and two dogs, while Anjelica Huston joins
up as the severe, calculating Director.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:23.020
Mark Dacascos will play the nefarious Zero,
while comedy favorite Jason Mantzoukas will

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.900
play the oddly-named and undoubtedly weird
Tick Tock Man.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.760
Keanu Reeves has been a lifelong fan and practitioner
of martial arts, but few roles have been as

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.920
demanding of him as John Wick.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.659
Reeves went all in a nd spent three months
at a "John Wick boot camp" to work on firearms

00:05:38.659 --> 00:05:42.030
training, fight choreography, and driving
like a maniac.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:46.550
Some of the training involved Reeves working
on his drawing, holstering, and even search-and-seizure

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.060
techniques.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.740
This helped him and the stunt team come up
with a unique style of movement and gunplay.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.900
No one moves quite like John Wick.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.800
Reeves is also heavily involved in the stunts.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:02.020
It'll be a wild ride to see how the stunt
team — and stuntmen-turned-filmmakers Chad

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.460
Stahelski and David Leitch — up the ante
for Chapter 3 as John Wick's world only continues

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.409
to get wilder and more dangerous.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.689
One of the best things about the secretive
world of assassins and gigantic Super Mario

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:17.809
gold coins that's presented in the John Wick
movies is that there's just enough to let

00:06:17.809 --> 00:06:19.920
us know that there's plenty we haven't seen.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.130
Those looking for a slightly expanded version
of that world, however, may have something

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:24.880
to look forward to.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.820
There is currently a spin-off television show
in the works at Starz.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.499
Called The Continental, it will showcase a
new kind of adventure in the world of John

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:38.060
Wick, focusing on a brand new character who's
pulled into the world as the story unfolds.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.219
Starz has its eyes on making a television
show that captures the slick ferocity of the

00:06:43.219 --> 00:06:47.909
John Wick films and has tapped the original
co-directors and producers Chad Stahelski

00:06:47.909 --> 00:06:52.749
and David Leitch, as well as original writer
Derek Kolstad — and, of course, executive

00:06:52.749 --> 00:06:54.260
producer Keanu Reeves.

